      "problem": "In Mrs. Morgan's class, $\\frac{3}{5}$ of the students are girls, and $\\frac{1}{2}$ of the girls like to play soccer. What fraction of the students in the class are girls who like to play soccer?",
      "worked_solution": "To find out the fraction of the students in the class who are girls that like to play soccer, we need to multiply $\\frac{3}{5}$ by $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nWe multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3\\times 1}{5\\times 2}=\\frac{3}{10}\n$$\n\nSo, $\\frac{3}{10}$ of all students in the class are girls who like to play soccer.",
